From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:32:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] egl: enumerate the software device when it renders zink

A build with zink but no software rasterizer, such as Apple's, hides its
only EGL device from eglQueryDevicesEXT: the software device is listed only
under HAVE_SWRAST. Yet on a platform without DRM devices that device is the
one the surfaceless platform's DRM-less probe binds for zink, so it is the
device every surfaceless display there renders on.

A client that needs a display of its own cannot get one without it. Mesa
keeps one display per platform, native display and attribute list, and
does not count eglInitialize calls on it, so any other client in the
process that opens the default surfaceless display shares it and can
terminate it underneath. EGL_EXT_explicit_device keys a separate display by
its device, but only a device eglQueryDevicesEXT lists can be named.

List the software device when zink is built as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/egl/main/egldevice.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/egl/main/egldevice.c b/src/egl/main/egldevice.c
index ebebda46efedc0131395521b92535769261e028c..8032e66e3aaab2460e3a4168e304c6e7e009cb3e 100644
--- a/src/egl/main/egldevice.c
+++ b/src/egl/main/egldevice.c
@@ -476,7 +476,12 @@ _eglQueryDevicesEXT(EGLint max_devices, _EGLDevice **devices,
    num_devs = _eglDeviceRefreshList();
    devs = _eglGlobal.DeviceList;
 
-#ifdef HAVE_SWRAST
+   /* Without a software rasterizer the software device still renders zink
+    * where there is no DRM device: the surfaceless platform's DRM-less probe
+    * binds it for zink. List it in that build too, so EGL_EXT_explicit_device
+    * can name the device such a display renders on.
+    */
+#if defined(HAVE_SWRAST) || defined(HAVE_ZINK)
    swrast = devs;
 #else
    swrast = NULL;
